.SH NAME
CWE\-280 \- Improper Handling of Insufficient Permissions or Privileges
.SH RANK
KEV\-referenced weakness. Not part of the 2025 CWE Top 25; documented here because it appears in the CISA KEV catalog.
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: KEV\-referenced weakness.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The product does not handle or incorrectly handles when it has insufficient privileges to access resources or functionality as specified by their permissions. This may cause it to follow unexpected code paths that may leave the product in an invalid state.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB1\fR exploited CVE mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
.SS CVE\-2024\-29748
Android Pixel, added 2024\-04\-04.
.PP
Android Pixel Privilege Escalation Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
Android Pixel contains a privilege escalation vulnerability that allows an attacker to interrupt a factory reset triggered by a device admin app.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply mitigations per vendor instructions, or discontinue use.
 Due 2024\-04\-25.
.PP
